just in tonight from the clark county  school district absentee among staff  members take a look at these numbers  this week the district reporting  1502 absences again for staff compared  to the return from that five-day pause  on friday january 21st the district saw  1571 absences but the highest number  coming in the friday before president's  day with the number of staff  missing work at 1  854. that number showing teacher  absences are actually growing  especially on mondays and fridays mary  jane bellies is sharing why some  teachers are not in the classroom  the clark county school district  collects teacher and student absence  numbers weekly but it doesn't explain  the reasons for those absences teachers  i spoke with say it's a combination of  sickness dealing with violent incidents  and simply being burnt out kristen nigro  is a teacher at steve shore elementary  school people are still testing positive  it might not be as much as what we have  seen in the past um but i also too  people are extremely nervous that even  if they get a slight tickle in their  throat or if they sneeze and cough  they're more you know apt to be at home  rather than come in and try to infect  everybody else vicki kreidel the  president of the national education  association of southern nevada says the  growing number of violent incidents at  schools have many teachers scared to  come to work if a teacher comes to me  and says i can't take it anymore i can  recommend you know care solas try to get  them some help sometimes they end up  going off on fmla because  it's too much to top it all off krydell  says teachers are simply burnt out most  of the people who are telling me they're  resigning are resigning to leave  education and that's what scares me  they're not leaving to go work at  another district because there isn't any  other districts here nigro anticipates  the teacher absence numbers will drop as  the weather gets warmer the weather  being nice and people coming back to  school we're you know really close to  spring break too  so we just gotta as educators power  through the rest of the school year and  put this one in the books this is  definitely one for the books the staff  absences have also caused another  problem a shortage in substitute  teachers a new regulation passed by the  department of education does permit over  500 emergency subs to teach in clark and  washoe county schools for the remainder  of this school year and next year if  nevada remains under a state of  emergency  we also reached out to the school  district ccsd saying it supports the  department of education's decision to  have emergency subs adding quote with  the nationwide teacher shortage school  districts across the state and country  must utilize every option to pair  teachers with students to raise academic  performance and satisfy the social  emotional well-being of our students
 

